From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hotschmoe <isaac@mass-engineering.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 08:37:31 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] misc: armchina-npu: limit cache maintenance to the requested
 buffer

aipu_mm_cache_flush() and aipu_mm_cache_invalid() ignore the buffer in the
request and clean or invalidate the whole memory region that contains it,
one cache line at a time. libnoe issues both around every job, and for
ResNet-50 each call took ~21 ms: 42 of the 47 ms per inference, while the
NPU itself finished in ~3 ms.

Translate buf->pa/buf->bytes into the VA range inside the region and
maintain only that; an empty or out-of-range request still covers the
region.

ResNet-50 (1 core), 200 inferences: 9.9 s -> 1.18 s at 1.2 GHz (CIX's
vendor kernel: 1.10 s). All outputs equal to the golden data.

Signed-off-by: hotschmoe <isaac@mass-engineering.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/misc/armchina-npu/aipu_mm.c | 30 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 28 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/misc/armchina-npu/aipu_mm.c b/drivers/misc/armchina-npu/aipu_mm.c
index 03d34a500..1c40f45db 100755
--- a/drivers/misc/armchina-npu/aipu_mm.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/armchina-npu/aipu_mm.c
@@ -1664,6 +1664,26 @@ static void tensor_flush_dcache_range(void *start, void *end) {
 
 }
 
+/*
+ * VA range of the buffer @buf names inside @reg. The cache ioctls used to
+ * clean or invalidate the whole region on every call (~21 ms per call for
+ * the ResNet-50 regions); an empty or out-of-range request still does.
+ */
+static void aipu_mm_buf_va_range(struct aipu_mem_region *reg, struct aipu_buf_desc *buf,
+				 void **start, void **end)
+{
+	u64 reg_end = reg->base_iova + reg->bytes;
+	u64 lo = buf->pa;
+	u64 hi = buf->pa + buf->bytes;
+
+	if (!buf->bytes || hi < lo || lo < reg->base_iova || hi > reg_end) {
+		lo = reg->base_iova;
+		hi = reg_end;
+	}
+	*start = reg->base_va + (lo - reg->base_iova);
+	*end = reg->base_va + (hi - reg->base_iova);
+}
+
 /**
  * @aipu_mm_cache_flush() - invald buffer allocated by aipu_mm_alloc()
  * @mm:   pointer to memory manager struct initialized in aipu_init_mm()
@@ -1687,8 +1707,11 @@ int aipu_mm_cache_flush(struct aipu_memory_manager *mm, struct aipu_buf_desc *bu
 	}
 
 	if(mm->has_iommu) {
+		void *start, *end;
+
+		aipu_mm_buf_va_range(reg, buf, &start, &end);
 		mutex_lock(&mm->lock);
-		tensor_flush_dcache_range(reg->base_va, (void *)reg->base_va + reg->bytes);
+		tensor_flush_dcache_range(start, end);
 		mutex_unlock(&mm->lock);
 	}
 
@@ -1718,8 +1741,11 @@ int aipu_mm_cache_invalid(struct aipu_memory_manager *mm, struct aipu_buf_desc *
 	}
 
 	if(mm->has_iommu) {
+		void *start, *end;
+
+		aipu_mm_buf_va_range(reg, buf, &start, &end);
 		mutex_lock(&mm->lock);
-		tensor_dcache_inval_poc(reg->base_va, (void *)reg->base_va + reg->bytes);
+		tensor_dcache_inval_poc(start, end);
 		mutex_unlock(&mm->lock);
 	}
 
-- 
